ameterization to a quarter-ellipse, we associate the parameter $\\theta $ with the central angle formed by a point $(x,y)$ on the elipse and the $x$-axis. \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040724/assets/9e236591e21403bb739dafa68a665c8a10eed0e9e8ac104e7b39431f02329c17.png)\n\nWe can see that if we restrict $\\theta $ to $[\\pi ,\\frac{3\\pi }{2}]$, we get the quarter-ellipse.\n\nTherefore, the parametric equations of the quarter-ellipse are \n\n$$\nx=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=3\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,\\theta \\in [\\pi ,\\frac{3\\pi }{2}].\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-106403/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9b51a7bc-7701-539f-9e20-dfc7f2574559"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-106403"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-79275/selection/254f7dc7c93945f5d800c08002268b921573aada24b982a69940059f541d28cc" :answer/id #uuid "df391d42-12ee-5fa3-967a-e1f130edceae" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\theta \\in [0,\\frac{\\pi }{2}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79275/selection/869e92fa37d662618b5776b5688120805f6a4ef64944d68a09668a86e88acb88" :answer/id #uuid "5e4925a6-7674-5878-9fcd-e3b2dd4b0a79" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\theta \\in [\\pi ,\\frac{3\\pi }{2}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79275/selection/5bda35dc7fabc5f84da2118d36bbe7c90786c71810c1d882ae9f6c6935b490ae" :answer/id #uuid "d257910b-fa78-51ab-a6bf-8d117abbe168" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\theta \\in [\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\frac{3\\pi }{2}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79275/selection/4205b99be199dc7950356b855ff4a5477c48c73878a7b026d25c035dbf46acb5" :answer/id #uuid "83cf8f2b-d3b0-5343-84ce-e680b7d0eef8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\theta \\in [0,\\pi ]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79275/sel