 parameterization to a semi-ellipse, we associate the parameter $\\theta $ with the central angle formed by a point $(x,y)$ on the elipse and the $x$-axis. \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040724/assets/5d615d9fd29a09345b05ee4d80ffdc49198924d0cd44edb9c815270543fae60f.png)\n\nWe can see that if we restrict $\\theta $ to $[0,\\pi ]$, we get the semi-ellipse.\n\nTherefore, the parametric equations of the semi-ellipse are \n\n$$\nx=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=4\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,\\theta \\in [0,\\pi ].\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-79275/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9b51a7bc-7701-539f-9e20-dfc7f2574559"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-79275"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-327835/field-1/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "ff9500fe-9439-59cc-989f-246dfe19b834" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-327835/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "de2c2553-ddc3-5ab2-929e-9e7280716de5" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-327835/field-1/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer-field/choices ["q-327835/field-1/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-327835/field-2/29ec2dfefa1bd3742bf5ba922b9c261dd5f2325bd8484e9153eb979dbd6eced6" :answer/id #uuid "9113ea42-9862-558c-acaf-88fcb1a0ee68" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\pi" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-327835/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "3c6c872a-33e3-5897-a566-49577106fa71" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-327835/field-2/29ec2dfefa1bd3742bf5ba922b9c261dd5f2325bd8484e9153eb979dbd6eced6" :answer-field/choices ["q-327835/field-2/29ec2dfefa1bd3742bf5ba922b9c261dd5f2325bd8484e9153eb979dbd6eced6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-327835" :question/id #uuid "72b22524-b982-564c-8317-a3f4cf8d743c" :question/math-academy-id "q-327835" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040724/assets/6f983fda4328227558e46aaaec454db2ccc0611331495c923ad1d90c7cb3df8a.png)\n\nThe semi-ellipse above is defined by the parametric equations \n\n$$\nx=8\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=3\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\nWhat is the domain of the parameter $\\theta ?$ Assume $\\theta $ is between $0$ and $2\\pi .$\n\n$\\theta \\in [${{field-1}},\n{{field-2}}$]$" :question/worked-solution "The parametric equations of an ellipse centered at the origin with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ are\n\n$$\nx=a\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=b\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ).\n$$\n\nIn our case, $a=8$ and $b=3.$ Therefore, the parametric equations of the *full* ellipse are\n\n$$\nx=8\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=3\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ).\n$$\n\nTo restrict the parameterization to a semi-ellipse, we associate the parameter $\\theta $ with the central angle formed by a point $(x,y)$ on the ellipse and the $x$-axis. \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040724/assets/101d9b26027bc5667009b0c7af69fa190c987c362122402fce62daec5833092f.png)\n\nWe can see that if we restrict $\\theta $ to $[0,\\pi ]$, we get the semi-ellipse.\n\nTherefore, the parametric equations of the semi-ellipse are \n\n$$\nx=8\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=3\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,\\theta \\in [0,\\pi ].\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-327835/field-1" "q-327835/field-2"] :db/ensure [:q